and only, Megan Thee Stallion.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.701
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:13.534
-"Traumazine." "Traumazine"
is out at midnight tonight.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.200
And we have a special guest
appearing.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.667
-Yes, 4oe!
-4oe! Welcome!

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.300
-He's like, "What's happening?
What's all these people?"

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.767
-4oe, look over there.
Look at the camera.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.100
-Who's that, 4oe?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.801
Who is that, 4oe? Who is that?

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.200
-He's so cute.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.601
-He's still there.
He's like, "Who is that?"

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.968
-He's a natural.

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.200
Thank you for being here.
Thanks for doing this.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.901
I appreciate it.
Do you have any questions

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.334
you want to ask me while you're
here 'cause you're co-hosting?

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:50.734
-Okay. So, the only question
that I really had was,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:54.267
are you a fan of Hot Cheetos?

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.968
-Of course.
-Okay.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.367
So, apparently, this is
like a thing

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.934
that I've only ever seen
in Houston happen.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:04.000
We eat Hot Cheetos
but inside of pickles.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.367
-I've never --

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.567
-Y'all have never done that
before?

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.467
-Has anybody done that?
Hot Cheetos inside?

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.934
-Inside of a pickle.
-Do we have one?

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:15.367
-So, we got these.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.534
-It's all gourmet.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:20.167
-Dude, look at you.
The best co-host ever.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.968
-This one's going to be mine.
And this one's for you.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.601
-Wait, look at this.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.534
-Yes.
-Now, this really is a thing?

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:31.601
Did you invent this?
-No, I promise, as a kid --

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.667
We can cheers it.
-Cheers.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.234
-Ting.
-Ting.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.400
-And just bite it.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.634
-Hey, I love it.
-I wouldn't lie to you.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.467
-I love that you just introduced
me to something awesome.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.133
Thank you so much, pal.
-Where are you going?

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.734
-I'm going to do that.
4oe, sorry, I couldn't save

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.801
anything for you.
-Let me take a sip of this water

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.734
before 4oe does.
-That is --

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.434
Is this mike on?

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:09.801
[ Dog breathing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.400
-Okay, usually 4oe shakes his
head like "No,"

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.601
when he doesn't like something.
He's just being shy tonight.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:17.968
-I like that.
-I'm like, "4oe, do you want

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.634
some vegetables"
and he'll be like...

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.934
-No, can I see if he'll sit
and give me his paw?

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:24.000
-Yeah. Oh, he will.
He gives high fives.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.801
-Pretty cute if he'll do it.
Ready?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.534
4oe, 4oe, sit.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:30.701
That's it, bud.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.400
-Such a good dog!

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.300
-Come on, that dog is talented.
Come on.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.067
He's so cute.
-That's my bestie.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.934
-He sits and gives a high five.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.000
Speaking of Hot Cheetos, though,
is it true Jay-Z

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.234
gave you a plate of Hot Cheetos
when he first signed you?

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:55.667
-Yes. Okay, so, everybody
on the entire planet knows

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.400
I'm like Miss Hot Cheetos.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.200
Even before I got a deal with
Hot Cheetos.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.601
I'm just obsessed with
Hot Cheetos.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:03.567
I would eat them for breakfast
in like middle school.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:07.267
So I feel like always on my
rider there's Hot Cheetos.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.701
Anytime I come in a room,

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.534
this room better be full of
Hot Cheetos.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.567
So I was in my meeting.

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.167
I was just about to sign with
Roc Nation.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.701
I hadn't signed my deal yet,
but I'm in the meeting

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:18.501
and I'm talking and everybody's
like, "Yeah, okay,

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.701
the boss is about to come in,"
and I'm like, "Who?"

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:24.467
And I look and it's Jay-Z.
And I'm like, "Uh!

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:26.634
Now Jay-Z in my meeting?"

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:27.801
-You didn't know
he was gonna be there?

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:30.501
-No, and it was like platters of
Hot Cheetos.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:34.634
And I was like, "Oh, I was gonna
sign anyway, but yes!"

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:40.701
That's how you do it.
-"Came right into my world."

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:43.000
I just want to say some things
that you've done since last time

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.300
you've been on the show, okay.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.434
You've won three Grammys,
by the way. Congratulations.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
I loved it.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:52.934
Best New Artist, Best Rap Song,
Best Rap Performance.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:55.200
You were named
top female rap artist

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.033
at the Billboard Music Awards
two years in a row, bud.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:01.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:04.934
You had multiple-platinum hit
songs with Cardi B,

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.567
seven times, by the way,
platinum.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.534
-It's almost diamond.
-Wow, diamond.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:11.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's amazing.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.267
You graduated college.
-Whoo!

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:20.868
And then you became
the first female rapper ever

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.734
to perform at the Oscars.
Come on.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.667
-What did that feel like?

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:32.167
-So, technically, Queen Latifah
is the first female rapper

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.167
to perform at the Oscars ever,

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.767
but she didn't perform
a rap song.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:38.601
So I'm the first female rapper
to perform a rap song.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:42.501
-Ah, that's good.
-Which is still really big.

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:46.434
-No, no, no, that's history.
-That's history.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.033
That was the first time that had
ever happened in life.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.601
And what's even more cool about
it is right before

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.801
I went on stage, I had no idea
Queen Latifah was there.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.133
So right before I went on stage,
I'm like backstage,

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.667
and I'm really nervous because
oh, my gosh, everybody in

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.300
Hollywood that's important
is in this one room

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.801
and they all about
to be looking at me.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:07.734
But Queen Latifah is in the back
and I'm like looking down

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:10.400
at my feet like, "Okay, Megan,
don't forget your lines."

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.000
And I look up and it's
Queen Latifah! And I'm like --

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:18.601
-You're like, "I'm nervous.
What do I do?"

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:20.634
-Lord, how do you add
more pressure on to

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.634
what I'm about to do right now?
Boom, Queen Latifah is in here.

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.000
-She's right there.
-She's right there.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.467
So, she's like -- you know like
the Spider-Man meme --

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:30.133
We both had on the same color
too, and people say

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.467
me and Queen Latifah look alike,
so I was just like,

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.801
"Oh, my gosh, yes, my girl,"
and she's like,

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.467
"Okay, I was about to leave,
but actually,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.868
because you here, you're about
to perform, I'm about to stay.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.734
So I was like, "Oh, yes!"

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.634
-Yeah, there's no one cooler.

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:43.067
-Nobody cooler than
Queen Latifah.

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.601
-She's the greatest. Here's
you two right here backstage.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:48.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.400
I love you, Latifah.
She's the greatest.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.167
And that was awesome.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.667
I also saw a photo you got with
Bill Murray

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.501
at one of the Oscar parties.
-Yes.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:57.801
-I was like, "Do you know Bill?"

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:02.000
You know Bill?
-I was gonna make sure

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.834
I knew him that day.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:05.167
"I need a picture with Bill."

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:08.267
-It was so random. I was like by
Tracee Ellis Ross,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.934
Chloe Bailey, a bunch of other
cool people,

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:14.767
and Bill Murray is just walking
by and I'm like...

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.567
"Y'all, I'mma get this picture
with Bill Murray.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.434
I'mma be right back."

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.067
-He's the best, man.
-I just ran up on him.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:23.300
I'm like, "Bill Murray, can I
take a picture?"

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.868
I don't know if he knew
who I was.

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:26.234
-Yeah, he does.
-Where you going?

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:29.334
-He's alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:33.667
-He's like, "I'm out.
Cut the check."

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.701
-Yeah, he's gonna go --
Bill Murray's in the hallway.

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:37.968
He's gonna go take a picture
with Bill.

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:40.133
Can we talk about "Traumazine"?

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.601
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.968
-This is a huge deal.
-This is out at midnight.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:45.601
This is out basically right now.
-Yes.

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:47.767
-It's out.
-It's out!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.667
-You've been teasing the album
for a while now.

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:54.400
It's finally out. How do you
know when an album's ready?

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.534
-I feel like it just feels good.

00:06:56.534 --> 00:07:00.267
Like, I literally -- This is
the longest time I've ever taken

00:07:00.267 --> 00:07:01.667
to record an album.

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:05.601
Like, I had at least 50 songs
recorded for this.

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:07.801
-Oh, my gosh.
-And we only chose 18.

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:10.567
-How do you do that?
-It was hard because --

00:07:10.567 --> 00:07:14.801
As an artist sometimes, like,
your label can kind of try to

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.300
control you and tell you
what to do. Like...

00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:20.634
And they kind of pick your songs
for you.

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:24.267
But I feel like I made it
a point to write all songs

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:26.434
that I loved and I liked
and that meant something to me

00:07:26.434 --> 00:07:28.968
so out of however many songs
I wrote,

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:31.000
all of them feel good to me.
-Yeah, so you could

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.868
put out an album of 50.
-Right.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:34.734
I could put all 50 of
those songs

00:07:34.734 --> 00:07:36.067
and they still mean
something to me.

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:38.100
-So where do those other songs
go, in the vault?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.100
-They go in the vault
but I think -- I'll do stuff

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.767
like release mix tapes
and things like that

00:07:41.767 --> 00:07:43.701
just to keep my hotties
on their toes, like,

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.634
"Hey, I'mma about to drop
something."

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:47.567
-You said this is
your most personal

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:50.467
and honest album to date.
-Yeah.

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:54.601
Writing this album, I treated it
more like writing in my diary

00:07:54.601 --> 00:07:57.868
than actually trying to put
together a song.

00:07:57.868 --> 00:07:59.834
-Yeah, like putting together
a song, you mean like

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.033
when you're writing a song,
"oh, this is catchy

00:08:02.033 --> 00:08:03.367
and this is gonna be a thing."

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:04.901
But this one, you're like,
"I just want to say this."

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:06.734
-I just want to talk about
how I really feel

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.267
and get more personal
with my hotties.

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:11.200
I feel like everybody knows me
and they have like a perception

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.634
of me based on probably what
other people say or what they

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:16.834
see on the Internet
or, you know, just --

00:08:16.834 --> 00:08:19.133
It's something that's probably
not me at all.

00:08:19.133 --> 00:08:21.267
And I feel like this time
around, I wanted to, like,

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.734
let everybody in my head
and, like, you know,

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:27.300
form their own opinion
based off of my story.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.000
I wanted to take control of
my own narrative.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:29.834
-Yeah.

00:08:29.834 --> 00:08:31.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:34.701
I think it's important
as an artist to do that.

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:35.834
-Yeah.
-Stretch yourself.

00:08:35.834 --> 00:08:37.734
But I heard you on the radio

00:08:37.734 --> 00:08:39.000
and I saw some video
the other day.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.434
You were freestyling.
-Yes.

00:08:40.434 --> 00:08:42.100
-Man, oh, man, can you rap.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.200
-I mean, I might be
a good rapper or whatever.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.601
-Yeah, "or whatever."

00:08:45.601 --> 00:08:47.734
It was unbelievable.

00:08:47.734 --> 00:08:49.634
And I freaked out.
"Yeah, show them how it's done."

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:51.667
-I might not have an Oscar,
you know.

00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:53.300
-Oh, yeah, some people have
the Oscar.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.033
-Some people have Oscars.
-Yeah, yeah, that's right.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:57.801
-I'm gonna get one.
I'm coming for it.

00:08:57.801 --> 00:08:59.534
-Yeah, of course you are.

00:08:59.534 --> 00:09:02.334
I figure since "Traumazine" is
actually officially,

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:05.167
officially out right now, let's
do a little champagne toast.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:07.000
-Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:08.634 --> 00:09:10.133
-This is a big deal.
-Okay.

00:09:10.133 --> 00:09:11.400
-So here we go. Alright.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.868
-You fancy.
-Should I do it?

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:17.033
-You got to shake it.
Just act like you in the club.

00:09:17.033 --> 00:09:19.334
Yeah, pop the bottle, Jimmy.
-I know, but --

00:09:19.334 --> 00:09:22.767
-Pop one, Jimmy. Give him
something to turn up to.

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:24.667
♪♪
-This is what I do in the club.

00:09:24.667 --> 00:09:25.701
-This is what you do
in the club.

00:09:25.701 --> 00:09:27.133
-Shake it up?
-Shake it up.

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.968
